[Music]  hi my name is gloria calderon khaled i  am the executive producer creator and  showrunner of with love  and my mantra is if you can't see it be  it so someone else can see it and that  really comes from my time in hollywood  where when i was coming up there were  not a lot of women and definitely not a  lot of latina women who were doing what  i wanted to do and so i thought well if  i don't have one role model i will  compile many and then if i make it then  hopefully i can be a role model to  someone else so that's kind of how it  all came about and now there's so many  more  women in hollywood that are doing this  so many women of color that are creating  their own shows and it's a really  exciting time  [Music]  yes and no i knew i wanted to be a  storyteller but i didn't know what that  looked like because i didn't know  writing was even a job directing was  even a job i knew acting because that  was what you see on the screen  so when i first came to los angeles i  thought oh i want to be an actor and  then the more i got into the industry  the more i was frustrated by the lack of  roles for women  and i decided to start writing my own  and then as i started writing i found a  new joy and a new way to express myself  and then when i got on sets i saw what  the director was doing and i thought oh  that seems really interesting too so i  started directing and now  directing writing producing and acting  are really what i do and it kind of  blows my mind that i get to do all of  that it's awesome  [Music]  i think the thing to know about the  industry is that it takes time  especially if you don't know anyone  there i didn't know anyone my parents  knew nothing about hollywood i grew up  in portland oregon uh so it was all a  mystery to me  and i think that a lot of people come to  hollywood and they're like i'm gonna  give it six months  and you gotta you gotta be committed to  this like you would be committed to  becoming a lawyer and putting in a  decade or being a doctor and putting in  a decade this takes a decade in my case  decades i started in hollywood when i  was 22 and now i'm 46 and i have the  life of my dreams now but it took this  long and that's okay  so i think this next generation is so  exciting because there's so much talent  so much energy but give yourself the  grace of time in that time you're gonna  learn so much and it's okay you don't  have to be defined by what your job is  right now the journey is just as  important as the destination  [Music]  oh gosh i would like my legacy to be  creating spaces for people that have not  traditionally got to be in those spaces  i think that there's a really exciting  thing happening in television right now  where  people who haven't always had the story  centered on them are starting to be the  face of their own show those are the  shows i'm most interested in right now  are seeing a different point of view  a different person from a different  culture sharing their story and what  their journey is and i think the more we  create space for that the more it unites  us and allows us to really see  how much like we are and in these very  divided times those are the stories that  make me feel connection so i hope my  legacy would be that i contributed to  that that i contributed to the building  of bridges with my work  i hope my mantra has inspired you today  and that you know that every part of  this journey is an amazing part  [Music]

